WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.275
Reading the findings is where
the rules become concrete.

2
00:00:03.275 --> 00:00:06.725
Every decision here is the
owner's, from Chapter 3.

3
00:00:06.725 --> 00:00:10.798
One web server account is trusted
for unconstrained delegation,

4
00:00:10.798 --> 00:00:15.852
which stops working after a delegated
migration, so its owner kept it on Kerberos,

5
00:00:15.852 --> 00:00:20.000
with the authorizing official's
acceptance, but it has no S P N owner.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.831
Two group accounts still name
computer accounts as retrievers,

7
00:00:23.831 --> 00:00:28.675
while their reviewed lists name one group
of hosts each, so the plan corrects both.

8
00:00:28.675 --> 00:00:32.138
An intranet account being
re-platformed has no owner

9
00:00:32.138 --> 00:00:35.287
and an end date years out,
so it can't be reconciled.

10
00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:40.050
Meanwhile the plan completes a migration
that started forty days ago, and creates

11
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:44.813
two group accounts with a thirty-day interval;
the print account's is outbound-only.

12
00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:48.580
Each write shows its request,
its change, and who sends it.
